                <pb facs="0850" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg751"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2222/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-30">October 30, 1936—[?] p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October
                        30—8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>X–266. Decree of Ministry of War, dated October 29, published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gaceta de Madrid</hi> today, makes liable for military
                    service all male Spaniards 20 to 45 years of age inclusive. I have addressed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">note verb ale</hi> to Ministry of State requesting that
                    Spanish employees of the Embassy and Consulate be exempted from provisions of
                    this decree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
